# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4-seats8-262k window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/seats8-262k and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN.
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. A placeholder in @...@ is filled in by
# whoever drives the window (zot.thatch.local:5000/tt-vllm:qwen38-c2-tp4-w1-1: the served image's reference; /home/thatch/opgraft-K64j and 152951c1c0de5c9dfad2d62c295393a43b2ecf353965c55c709da7e539b975b7: the K64j graft
# directory and its binary's digest, the one-card harnesses); every other value is final. ORDER.txt says the order, each job's
# image, its stop rule and its minutes.
# DEFERRED (the owner skipped the single-card evidence run: the quad-first window runs on the gate-only evidence waiver instead; this job stays in the pack, after the quad jobs).
# STAGE 1 of the 262k window (the I2 evidence): card M alone through the cardm action (C2_CARDS=pair: cardm is a pair-shaped step), the
# harness being this checkout's own code run in the I1 base image, so no new image is needed. Production is DOWN from A0 to the hand-back.
# An EVIDENCE job: one harness on card M alone (the quad jobs reset all four boards, this one never does). The harness runs its own
# image and mounts this checkout's scripts as the code under test. The K64j graft binary is pinned by EXPECT_TTNNCPP_SHA256: read the
# launched argv, a graft mounted is not a graft executed. A watcher job (W) runs before its full job; a REDUCED-PASS or a reduced scope
# is never evidence. A FAIL or a NO-DECISION here blocks the 262k window pending kernel work; I1 (eight 131k seats) is unaffected.
# E1: the same at full scope: both writers, both widths, seeds 0, 1 and 2, the three cases (eager; replay_changed, the page table rewritten
# in place between replays; replay_unchanged) and the complete-cache readback after every step against the cache predicted on the host
# from the host page table alone (predicted blocks exact, every other block still zero; an extra write fails as surely as a missing one).
# Page-table entries cycled by every row: 0, 1, 1023, 1024, 2047, 2048, 2051, 2052, 3071, 4094, 4095; the last step puts rows 0-31 on
# positions 262,080-262,111. page_width_tp4.admitted is patched to admit exactly 4,096 for the run only (the report records the patch).
# PASS: 'ORDERED_WRITER verdict=PASS scope=full width=4096 chips=1of4 ...'. Then scripts/ci/record_ordered_writer_evidence_tp4.py writes
# ordered_writer_evidence_tp4.json and ORDERED_WRITER_EVIDENCE_TP4_SHA256 together; commit both by path.
# Duration (estimate): 15-25 min runner time (about 450 readbacks of the 71 MB cache). Stop rule: a FAIL or NO-DECISION blocks 262k.
C2_CARDS=pair
C2_ACTIONS=cardm
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-w1-1
C2_CARDM_HARNESS=optimisation/ttnn-op/k64j/run_card_b.sh
C2_CARDM_ARGS=--widths 2052,4096 --writers chained64,tiles32 --seeds 0,1,2
C2_CARDM_ENV=K64J_HARNESS=ordered_writer IMAGE=zot.thatch.local:5000/tt-vllm:qwen38-c2-tp4-w1-1 KOPGRAFT64=/home/thatch/opgraft-K64j EXPECT_TTNNCPP_SHA256=152951c1c0de5c9dfad2d62c295393a43b2ecf353965c55c709da7e539b975b7
